    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter August 24th prioritizing high-upside matchups, headlined by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13) and **Junior Caminero** (76.13). **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is our clear standout; facing Merrill Kelly\u2019s inflated 5.27 xERA, he benefits from a massive platoon advantage and a projected leadoff spot that maximizes his elite speed potential\u2014our primary objective in this 5x5 Roto chase. Similarly, **Junior Caminero** is locked into the #3 hole against Framber Valdez. While facing a lefty typically suppresses his ceiling, the favorable park factors and the premium lineup positioning buoy him well above our \"Strong\" start threshold. **Lars Nootbaar** (60.62) also secures a start, as his dynamic platoon edge against Kevin Gausman offsets the veteran righty's pedigree, demonstrating our commitment to playing the matchups over name-brand perception.\n\nThe most difficult benching decision involved **Dillon Dingler** (37.53), who fell just shy of our 40.0 \"Marginal\" floor. Despite a decent park factor and potential for wind-aided power against Rasmussen, the negative SP skill coefficient and suboptimal platoon splits against a right-handed arm made him a statistical fade compared to the reliable daily floor of **Caleb Durbin** (57.43). We are also navigating significant risk with **Trea Turner** (51.35) and **Kyle Schwarber** (50.87); both are relegated to marginal status today due to the formidable presence of Logan Gilbert on the mound. While we need their speed and power, their low scores reflect the reality of facing an elite arm that consistently suppresses production. We continue to monitor the status of **Pedro Ramirez** and **Pete Crow-Armstrong**; if their lineup positions drop significantly lower than projected, we will need to re-evaluate our approach to the middle infield and outfield configuration to protect our daily efficiency metrics.",
